// =============================================================================
// TeraTrip - Laboratorio 3
// Parte A: Ingesta inteligente de reservas desde documentos
//
// Pegar en https://app.eraser.io  ->  nuevo Diagram-as-code
// Exportar como SVG a docs/diagrams/parte_a_ingesta.svg
// =============================================================================

title Parte A - Ingesta inteligente de reservas

direction right

Analista [icon: user]

Data Lake S3 [icon: aws-s3, color: green] {
  incoming-documents [icon: file]
  textract-raw [icon: file]
  incoming-data [icon: file]
  curated booking_analytics [icon: database]
}

EventBridge [icon: aws-eventbridge, color: purple]

sfn-teratrip-ingest [icon: aws-step-functions, color: purple] {
  1 Extraer tabla [icon: aws-lambda]
  2 Normalizar [icon: aws-lambda]
  3 Hay registros [icon: git-branch]
  4 Merge curated [icon: aws-glue]
}

Amazon Textract [icon: aws-textract, color: orange]
Glue Data Catalog [icon: aws-glue]
Amazon Athena [icon: aws-athena, color: blue]

// --- Disparo automatico ---
Analista > incoming-documents: sube el PDF
incoming-documents > EventBridge: Object Created
EventBridge > 1 Extraer tabla: StartExecution

// --- Extraccion ---
1 Extraer tabla <> Amazon Textract: AnalyzeDocument TABLES
1 Extraer tabla > textract-raw: JSON crudo (debug)
1 Extraer tabla > 2 Normalizar: grilla + run_id del eTag

// --- Normalizacion ---
2 Normalizar > incoming-data: records.jsonl
2 Normalizar > 3 Hay registros

// --- Merge ---
3 Hay registros > 4 Merge curated: record_count > 0
4 Merge curated > curated booking_analytics: anti-join por booking_id

// --- Consulta ---
curated booking_analytics > Glue Data Catalog
Glue Data Catalog > Amazon Athena: teratrip_db.booking_analytics
